{%- comment -%}
  Renders "Only N left" for products that are nearly out of stock.

  Parameters:
    low_inventory_variant  optional variant. When set, the notice reports that
                           variant's remaining stock instead of the product
                           total. Product cards link to a whole product, so they
                           omit it; the product page passes the selected variant.
    low_inventory_persist  when true the element is always rendered, hidden
                           while stock is not low, so product-form.js can
                           refresh it after a variant change without having to
                           build markup of its own.

  The count is printed once stock is down to five units, except for the series
  named by low_inventory_show_all_handle below, which prints its count at every
  quantity.

  Remaining stock is only claimed when the platform reports a positive quantity.
  A product whose stock is not tracked reports nothing or zero, which is
  indistinguishable here from sold out, so no count is shown for it. Sold-out
  products keep their existing badge and add nothing.

  `include` shares one scope in EasyStore Liquid, so the parameters are reset at
  the end: without that, the product page's selected variant would still be set
  when the related-product cards below it render. `escape_output` belongs to
  translation-fallback and is reset for the same reason - the copy that follows
  this notice asked for the unescaped form.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% comment %} `| plus: 0` keeps every count a number: a product or variant that reports no quantity at all compares as nil, and comparing nil with a number is an error rather than a false on Liquid. {% endcomment %}
{% assign low_inventory_threshold = 5 %}
{% comment %}
  Products whose handle names this series advertise their stock the whole way
  down rather than only in their last five units, because each episode is a
  livestream and a live count is worth more to a shopper watching it than a
  notice that appears only in the last five units. It is matched anywhere in the
  handle, so every shape of the series is covered by the one value:
  'late-night-crackers-ep3', episodes not streamed yet, and
  'bundle-late-night-crackers-ep3', which carries the name in the middle of its
  handle. Case does not matter on either side, because EasyStore product URLs
  are lowercase even when the administrative value is capitalized. Blank leaves
  every product on the threshold above.

  The handle is read from the product's link as well as from product.handle,
  because a card is not given the same product object a product page is. The
  product page reads the product EasyStore loads in full, so the handle is
  always there and the series was recognised; a collection listing serializes
  less of it, and a card whose product arrived without a handle read as a
  product outside the series and went back to the five-unit threshold, which is
  why one of these products printed its count on its own page and on nothing
  else. Every card links to its product, so the link is the one place the handle
  is always spelled out.

  Only the segment after '/products/' is read, so a link written within a
  collection - '/collections/late-night-crackers/products/mtg-hob-cbb-en' -
  is matched on the product it points at and never on the collection it was
  written through. A link that names no product is ignored rather than matched
  whole, for the same reason. The SKU is read too, because this theme already
  identifies a product by either, as the purchase limits do.

  The identifiers are joined with '|' so that no match can be made across the
  join between one identifier and the next.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign low_inventory_show_all_handle = 'late-night-crackers' %}
{% comment %} The URL is lowered before it is split as well as after, so the '/products/' it is split on is found whatever case the link was written in. {% endcomment %}
{% assign low_inventory_url = product.url | default: '' | append: '' | downcase %}
{% assign low_inventory_url_handle = '' %}
{% if low_inventory_url contains '/products/' %}
  {% assign low_inventory_url_handle = low_inventory_url | split: '/products/' | last | split: '?' | first | split: '#' | first %}
{% endif %}
{% capture low_inventory_identity %}{{ product.handle }}|{{ low_inventory_url_handle }}|{{ product.sku }}{% endcapture %}
{% assign low_inventory_identity = low_inventory_identity | downcase %}
{% assign low_inventory_show_all = false %}
{% if low_inventory_show_all_handle != '' and low_inventory_identity contains low_inventory_show_all_handle %}
  {% assign low_inventory_show_all = true %}
{% endif %}
{% comment %}
  Stock is counted for a variant unless the platform says that variant cannot be
  bought. It is deliberately not the other way round: a variant is only dropped
  for a flag that reads false, never for a flag that is missing.

  A product page renders the product EasyStore loads in full, where a variant
  carries `available`. Collection, home, search, and cart listings render the
  product objects from a collection, which do not all carry that field - this
  theme's own card reads `variant.is_enabled` for its variant thumbnails, and
  EasyStore names the same idea `is_available` on order line items. Requiring
  `available` therefore counted nothing on a listing whose variants spell
  availability another way, and those cards fell back to the product-level total
  or, where the platform reports none, printed nothing at all while the product
  page printed a count. All three spellings are read here, and any of them
  reading false drops the variant.

  The count itself is still the gate that matters: a variant with no stock, or
  with stock the platform does not track, is excluded by its quantity below
  whatever its flags say.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign low_inventory_remaining = 0 %}
{% if low_inventory_variant %}
  {% assign low_inventory_count = low_inventory_variant.inventory_quantity | plus: 0 %}
  {% capture low_inventory_availability %}{{ low_inventory_variant.available }} {{ low_inventory_variant.is_available }} {{ low_inventory_variant.is_enabled }}{% endcapture %}
  {% assign low_inventory_availability = low_inventory_availability | downcase %}
  {% unless low_inventory_availability contains 'false' or low_inventory_availability contains '0' %}
    {% if low_inventory_count > 0 %}
      {% assign low_inventory_remaining = low_inventory_count %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endunless %}
{% elsif product.available %}
  {% for variant in product.variants %}
    {% assign low_inventory_count = variant.inventory_quantity | plus: 0 %}
    {% capture low_inventory_availability %}{{ variant.available }} {{ variant.is_available }} {{ variant.is_enabled }}{% endcapture %}
    {% assign low_inventory_availability = low_inventory_availability | downcase %}
    {% unless low_inventory_availability contains 'false' or low_inventory_availability contains '0' %}
      {% if low_inventory_count > 0 %}
        {% assign low_inventory_remaining = low_inventory_remaining | plus: low_inventory_count %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% comment %} Products that report stock on the product itself rather than per variant. {% endcomment %}
  {% assign low_inventory_count = product.inventory_quantity | plus: 0 %}
  {% if low_inventory_remaining == 0 and low_inventory_count > 0 %}
    {% assign low_inventory_remaining = low_inventory_count %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% assign low_inventory_is_low = false %}
{% if low_inventory_remaining > 0 %}
  {% if low_inventory_show_all or low_inventory_remaining <= low_inventory_threshold %}
    {% assign low_inventory_is_low = true %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% comment %} 'all' travels to product-form.js the same way a number does, so the script keeps printing the count after a variant change instead of hiding it at six units. {% endcomment %}
{% assign low_inventory_threshold_attribute = low_inventory_threshold %}
{% if low_inventory_show_all %}
  {% assign low_inventory_threshold_attribute = 'all' %}
{% endif %}
{% capture low_inventory_text %}{% include 'translation-fallback', translation_key: 'products.product.low_inventory', fallback: 'Only __COUNT__ left', escape_output: true %}{% endcapture %}
{% assign low_inventory_text = low_inventory_text | strip | replace: '__COUNT__', low_inventory_remaining %}
{% if low_inventory_is_low or low_inventory_persist %}<span class="low-inventory-notice{% unless low_inventory_is_low %} hidden{% endunless %}" data-low-inventory-notice data-low-inventory-threshold="{{ low_inventory_threshold_attribute }}"{% unless low_inventory_is_low %} hidden="hidden"{% endunless %}{% if low_inventory_persist %} role="status" aria-live="polite"{% endif %}>{% if low_inventory_is_low %}{{ low_inventory_text }}{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}
{% assign low_inventory_variant = null %}
{% assign low_inventory_persist = null %}
{% assign escape_output = null %}
